  "body": "## Problem\n\nVinted can render model search results so both the selectable row and a nested title node match the prefix\n`selectable-item-brand_collection-`.\n\nThe current code accepts the known `--title` suffix as exact model evidence, but then clicks whichever exact locator was selected. That can click the text/title node instead of toggling the model checkbox. The UI then shows the exact model but leaves the checkbox empty.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Treat `--title` nodes as identity/text evidence only.\n- Resolve the proven collection id back to the canonical row:\n  `selectable-item-brand_collection-<id>`.\n- Prefer the checkbox inside that exact row:\n  - native `input[type=checkbox]`,\n  - then role=checkbox,\n  - then row label,\n  - finally the historical exact-row click fallback.\n- If a semantic checkbox exists, require a confirmed checked/selected state before clicking \"Pokaż wyniki\".\n- Final persistence remains fail-closed: the catalog URL still has to contain the exact proven `brand_collection_ids[]` value.\n- No fuzzy model matching is introduced; S25 / S25 FE / Edge / Ultra remain distinct.\n\n## Regression\n\nAdds a test proving title-child evidence is canonicalized back to the base selectable row id.\n",
